    "suggested_action": "quarantine",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'spare' is assigned as a verb. However, the Japanese expression '補用' (ほよう) is primarily a noun meaning 'supplementary use' or 'spare use'. While it can form a verbal noun with 'する' (補用する), '補用' itself is not a standalone verb. Furthermore, the JMdict glosses ('replacement', 'spare', 'extra') clearly refer to the noun/adjective concept of 'spare' (as in a spare part or extra item), not the common verb senses of 'spare' (e.g., to spare time, to spare a life, to refrain from harming). There is a fundamental mismatch in both part-of-speech and semantic meaning.",
